Tested-by: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@kernel.org>
Cc: Zi Yan <ziy@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by incorrectly setting search marks on all entries in a newly created node when splitting an entry that had search marks set. This behavior was appropriate for splits to order 0 but led to incorrect marking of sibling entries when splitting to a larger order, violating the intended logic of the XArray implementation.

Here is the patch:

+static inline void node_mark_slots(struct xa_node *node, unsigned int sibs,
+		xa_mark_t mark)
+{
+	int i;
